<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shughnan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shugnan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shughnan is a mountain district of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamir-mountains">Pamirs</a> on both banks of the Panj river, divided between Tajikistan, where Khorog is its main town, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. Its people speak Shughni, an Eastern Iranian language, and are mostly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> Muslims. Long ruled by its own shahs under the overlordship of Badakhshan, it was divided along the Panj by the Anglo-Russian Pamir agreement of 1895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shughnan.jpg" alt="Shughnan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khwahan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beautiful_view_of_Panj_river,_of_the_border_between_Afghanistan_and_Tajikistan_the_in_Shughnon-shughnan_region.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
